---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Privacy Policy — TubeTrainer';
const description = 'How TubeTrainer handles your data: local-first, no account, no analytics, no tracking.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/privacy">
  <section class="section prose-page">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>

      <p class="lead">
        TubeTrainer is built to need as little of your data as possible. There is no account, no server,
        and no analytics. Your workouts live on your device. This policy explains exactly what that means.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p><strong>The short version:</strong> We don’t collect, store, or sell your personal data.
        TubeTrainer has no backend and no tracking. The only time the app goes online is to find, preview,
        or play the YouTube coaching videos you choose.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        “TubeTrainer”, “we”, “us” refers to the developer of the TubeTrainer iOS app. This policy covers the
        TubeTrainer app and the tubetrainer.app website.
      </p>

      <h2>Data we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>None.</strong> TubeTrainer has no user accounts and no servers of our own. We do not collect,
        receive, or store your name, email, contacts, location, device identifiers, or your workout data.
      </p>

      <h2>Data the app stores on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Everything you create in TubeTrainer — your exercises, workouts, logged sets, history, notes,
        favourites, and the references to coaching videos you save — is stored <strong>locally on your
        device</strong> using Apple’s on-device database. It never leaves your device unless you choose to
        export a backup file yourself.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Backups</strong> you create are ordinary files saved wherever you send them (e.g. Files or
        AirDrop). You control them entirely; we never receive them.</li>
        <li><strong>Deleting the app</strong> removes this data from your device.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>YouTube &amp; Google</h2>
      <p>
        TubeTrainer helps you attach coaching videos from YouTube to your exercises. To do that, the app
        connects to YouTube/Google services to search for, preview, and play videos you select, and to fetch
        basic details like a title, channel name, and thumbnail. TubeTrainer stores only a <strong>reference</strong>
        to a video (such as its link and title) — never the video itself.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you view or play a YouTube video, or open one in YouTube, Google may receive information in
        accordance with its own privacy policy — the same as visiting YouTube in a browser. That processing is
        governed by <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>
        and the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener" target="_blank">YouTube Terms of Service</a>.
        We do not download, host, or redistribute any YouTube content.
      </p>
      <p>
        In-app video search is optional and only works if you add your own YouTube Data API key in Settings.
        If you do, that key is stored <strong>only on your device</strong> and is used solely to talk to
        Google’s YouTube service. We never see it.
      </p>

      <h2>Notifications</h2>
      <p>
        If you enable the rest-timer notification, TubeTrainer schedules a local notification on your device so
        it can alert you when a rest period ends. These are handled by iOS on your device; no notification data
        is sent to us.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics, advertising &amp; tracking</h2>
      <p>
        There are none. TubeTrainer contains no third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking SDKs, and does
        not use the Advertising Identifier (IDFA). We do not track you across apps or websites.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        TubeTrainer is a general-audience fitness app and is not directed at children under 13. Because we do
        not collect personal data, we do not knowingly collect data from anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Because your data stays on your device and we hold nothing about you, there is nothing for us to access,
        correct, or delete on our side. You are always in control: export your data at any time, and remove it
        by deleting the app.
      </p>

      <h2>The website</h2>
      <p>
        The tubetrainer.app website is a static marketing site hosted on Netlify. It sets no advertising or
        tracking cookies. Your colour-theme preference is stored in your browser’s local storage on your device
        and is never sent anywhere. Netlify may process standard, aggregated server logs (such as IP address and
        browser type) to deliver and secure the site, per <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Netlify’s privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, we’ll update this page and the “last updated” date above.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? See our <a href="/support">Support</a> page for ways to get in touch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
